<title>GERMANY: German car registrations 0.9 pct up in yr to July.</title>
<headline>German car registrations 0.9 pct up in yr to July.</headline>
<dateline>FLENSBURG, Germany 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The total number of cars registered in Germany was 0.9 percent higher as of July 1 compared with one year earlier, the Federal Motor Office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The office said some 41,371,992 cars were registered, with the strongest growth coming from east Germany where the number of registered cars climbed 1.6 percent. In west Germany, the figure increased 0.8 percent.</p>
<p>The total number of motor vehicles registered in Germany including motor cycles and trucks increased 1.6 percent to 53,424,141.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom + 49 228 26097150.</p>
